NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1021,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,3,4,2,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.0068,"rank":0.0948,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV000604","role":"target","render":{"description":"Urgent advice to take out fire insurance, because someone has seen the house on fire. Some time later the house burns down.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/42967","original":"[4.]\nMijn opa kwam ook eens bij buurman Scheper. \"Hest dien hoes in de brandkaaste Beernd?\"\n\"Nee,\" zei Beernd.\n'n Paor dagen later opa er weer heen.\n\"Beernd, hest 't hoes in de brandkaaste?\"\n\"Nee, nog nich.\"\n\"Dou hum d'r doadeluk in, want ik heb 't branden zain.\"\nEen paar maanden later, daor ging 't huis.","lang":"Standard Dutch; Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV005903","role":"helper","render":{"description":"When his farm burns down, a man says he saw the house on fire long beforehand but kept quiet about it.","place":"Wessingtange","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43264","original":"Veurloop.\nJoarn leden is hier brand west. Ik huilp de boer mit alles. De man stön aal man stil te kiekn en zee:“Nôn brand e ja.”\nIk vruig:“Hou komst door bie, wat betaikent dat?”\n“t Is wol al tien joar leden”, zee e dou, “op n oavend kwam k bie hoes en dou stôn alles in lichtelaaie. k Heb dr nooit over proot, mit ganaine, man nôn brand e ja.”","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.9175,7.14444]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV007406","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Lights are seen as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of fire.","place":"Musselkanaal","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44126","original":"Lichten zaggen ze vrouger voak. \"dr brandt weer wat\", zeden ze, zel wel weer gauw n huus aan goan. Dat geleuf was algemain.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.9325,7.01528]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV013008","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that all the white houses will burn down comes true; only the white church is still standing.","place":"Bourtange","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44092","original":"Oal vrouw K. zag vrouger ale widde huuzn in Boertange brannen.\n“Zai brant aal op”, zee ze. En t oal hef nog gliek kreegn ook. Allaind de widde kerke stait dr nog.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.01,7.19028]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Wessingtange.","Find Jipsingboertange on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[52.965,7.10139],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Jipsingboertange"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1418,"rank":0.2835,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ070902","role":"member","render":{"description":"People once saw a farm on fire. But when they came closer, nothing was wrong. Later the farm really burned down.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27979","original":"Myn wiif fortelde wolris dat to Sybrandahûs - tusken Dokkum en Rinsumageast - seagen lju yn 'e nacht in boereplaets yn 'e brân. Hja hearden allerhande lûden en stemmen fan minsken. Sy gongen der hinne, mar der wie neat.\nLetter is dy plaets troch de tonger opbrând.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ088406","role":"member","render":{"description":"A man once saw a farmhouse on fire, but when he came closer, nothing turned out to be wrong. Later the farm did burn down after all.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33288","original":"yn 'e brân. 't Wie by de earste bocht as men gyng fan 'e brêge fan 'e Harkema nei Surhústerfean. Mar doe't omke der by kom, brânde 't net.\nLetter is dat spul ôfbrând.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KEMP295","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A boy is released from being a werewolf when his pelt gets burnt. His friends helped him with this unintentionally.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43420","original":"De weerwolf verlost\n\nTe Blitterswijk woonde een jonge man die de naam had des nachts uit weerwolven te gaan. Enige vrienden wilden echter wel eens bij die gedaanteverwiseling tegenwoordig zijn. Zij gingen daarom een avond naar zijn huis en zetten zich om de haard. Het ging op middernacht aan en daar niemand sprak van naar huis gaan, zweette de weerwolf water en bloed van benauwdheid. Hij wilde de deur uit, maar zijn kameraden beletten hem dit en hielden hem stevig vast.\nToen het middernacht sloeg, viel opeens een groot wolfsvel uit de schoorsteen in het vuur. De weerwolf begon te schreeuwen als een bezetene en stelde zich aan als een duivel. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ037801","role":"member","render":{"description":"A boy and a girl once saw a fire from a distance, but when they came closer there was no fire at all. A year later a fire did break out at that spot.","place":"Kollum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/23086","original":"It is jierren lyn. Ik en myn feint kommen us fan Sweagerfean. Wy moesten nei de Triemen ta. Wy roannen de Úlke-loane del by Swagerfean. Doe't wy sahwat midden op 'e loane wienen, en oer de feart seagen, seinen wy: \"Sjoch, dêr is brân!\"\nDêr woenen wy hinne en sa kommen wy op 'e Trekwei. Mar dêr wie neat to sjen. Alles wie tsjuster.\nIn jier nei dy tiid briek dêr brân út op in pleats, krekt op datselde plak, dêr't wy de brân sjoen hienen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Broek belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.0771,"rank":0.0042,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ031107","role":"omen","render":{"description":"If a mirror falls down, someone will die within six weeks.","place":"Twijzelerheide","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21986","original":"As in spegel delkomt, komt der binnen seis wiken in sippe deaden.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CBAK0041","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Prediction that a child will not live long. The child indeed dies at the age of six.","place":"Broek in Waterland","prov":"N.-H.","year":1899,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/8638","original":"Grietje Holleman heeft tegen een broertje van een Broeker dame gezegd dat hij niet oud zou worden. Op zes-jarige leeftijd is hij overleden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV013104","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A corpse that lies unburied over a Sunday means another death within six weeks.","place":"Bellingwolde","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44380","original":"n Volksgeleuf was wieder, dat as ain liek n zundag overstun, dat er den binnen zes weekn weer ['n] staarfgeval komen zol.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","6 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":6},"on_success":{"chime":6,"digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.6258,"rank":0.0,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL000404","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Seeing a witte juffer (white lady); playing at being a witte juffer with a white sheet around oneself.","place":"Ingen","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209537","original":"Witte vrouwen . Bij de pas (aanplant van wilgen of populieren met onderhout van elzen en essen) (lag dicht bij de woning van de zegslieden) zag men soms een witte gedaante lopen. Maar sommigen geloofden niet aan de witte juffer, zo werd Han Briene er van verdacht, dat hij soms de kinderen bang wilde maken door voor witte juffer te spelen (hij deed zich dan een laken om) Enige jongens wilden met Jas Gaosbeek, een niet volwaardige zoon van een bakker, een grap uithalen. Zij sloegen zich lakens om en gingen wandelen op een plaats, waar Jas passeren moest. Deze ging er echter niet voor door, maar begon de \"juffer\", die hij het eerst te pakken kreeg af te ranselen. De andere jongens sloegen toen op de vlucht","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL002208","role":"variant","render":{"description":"In the evening, mistaking a stick with a newspaper on it for a witte juffer (white lady).","place":"Ochten","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210065","original":"Er moet een witte juffer gelopen hebben op het Zand (fruitteeltbedrijf) bij het witte hek (dit stond op de weg, die tussen twee kolken doorloopt. Keuken, hij was toen 18 jaar, ging eens met een kameraad naar Eldik (buurtschap) om een vriend te bezoeken. Deze bleek niet thuis. Op de dijk op de plaats waar beneden het witte hek stond, was een stok met krant er om gezet, als teken voor de castreur dat er \"keujes\" moesten gesneden worden. Janus stapte tegen deze stok aan, deze ging heen en weer, de kameraad beweerde, dat hij een witte juffer had gezien en was van dit idee, ook de volgende dag, niet af te brengen","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"HOL002604","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A white maiden who asks the way throws a hat full of money and disappears.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210163","original":"Berend, den dakuil (een Van Uden) smeerde de daken van binnen aan met kalk, vandaar dat hij deze bijnaam kreeg. Eens liep Berend op de Grotebrugse grintweg bij de Twaalf Apostelen (straatje) toen een witte juffer hem de weg vroeg naar het veer. Berend zei haar die en nadat hij dit gedaan had, gooide zij hem de hoed vol met \"Berliner daolder\". Driemaal was Berend dit overkomen. Bij het veer gekomen wilde Berend haar bedanken, maar hij kreeg geen kans daartoe: zij was verdwenen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Gelderland an object was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1962.","That card names an object. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"222e7416a6a8c788","accepted_hashes":["7b8db4a0c5068ec878f5142a1100338af870ab1cc7ed1e8cc1895b29f76b332f","83f25af6def383c641125a737f416ebe799f05a875513d23d60f23caf70cd3f5","890ca6681f7b0574d03096d9cc48f4754ef5cb1bfebc54841c50e0231e82c9ad","8d7314310d7408b55024f66883d0092df3d8ed18d4ca08f662c30465e7ddd6c8","8f9f1b21222aeb267a7cf549be587545d5a6a11a4d189e6e1188fa10cd85bfa8","ff3bc7f6b5efc58a8092d08e509acf2a7e5ec5e44b2a27207189368919ba004a"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.4374,"rank":1.1941,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ103913","role":"member","render":{"description":"One evening a man thought he recognised his niece in a woman coming towards him. However, he was lifted up and thrown away, after which the woman floated off.","place":"Drogeham","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37327","original":"It gebeurde op 'e Ikkers op in joun dat Harm Hamstra bûtendoar kaem en in frommeske seach. Hy miende dat it syn nichtsje wie, in jongfaem fan sa'n tweintich jier: Wytske Hamstra, dy't letter troude mei Elle Wijma fan Eastemar. Hja kaem him yn 'e mjitte.\nHy sei: \"Bistû dêr noch, Wytske?\"\nMar dyselde sei neat werom. Ynpleats dêrfan wied er opnom woarn en in ein fuortsmiten en dat frommeske wie swevend fuortrekke.\nOp 'e weromreis kom er wer by ús tolânne. 't Ljocht wie by ús noch op. Doe hat ús heit him dat út brocht hwant hy doarst dêr net wer allinne lâns.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ103307","role":"member","render":{"description":"A man once saw a woman in white approaching. Because he thought he knew her, he wanted to greet her, but when he came closer she went up in smoke.","place":"Drogeham","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37235","original":"In man fan Droegeham (it wie Hindrik Hoeksma sels) seach op in joun op 'e Ikkers in frommes yn 't wyt oankommen.\nHy miende dat er har wol koe en soe har groetsje. Mar doe't er flakby wie, wie se samar ynienen fuort troch in daem. Der wie neat mear fan har to sjen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"BIJLSMA000103","role":"member","render":{"description":"Early in the morning a man sees a white woman.","place":"Hemelum","prov":"Fr.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130174","original":"Oer de Lytse Maren sjocht men op ’e eftergroun de Wite Burch. Dêr seach men eren wite wiven. In man fan Himmelom, Melchers hjitte er, gie op in moarn ier en bitiid to ikeboskjen, en seach dêr yn in iepen plak tsjin de Wite Burch oan in wyt wiif omdoarmjen.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ053715","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A man once had an encounter. He was roughly thrown about by the figure.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25414","original":"Alde Rinse de Wind fan 'e Harkema hat ek us in ûntmoeting hawn. Dy waerd dêrby ek smiten.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Boornbergum belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.1119,"rank":0.9153,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ006015","role":"card","render":{"description":"In Den Andel there is a haunted barn. A woman has been seen at the window with a face as white as chalk and her hair hanging limp around it.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16534","original":"Yn Den Andel wie ek in spûkskuorre. De minsken dy't op dy pleats wennen, woarden sa binaud, dat se der wei gong binne. Der stienen allegear beammen om dy plaets hinne. Guon ha dêr wol in frommes foar it glês stean sjoen mei in holle sa wyt as kryt, en 't hier der sleau om hinne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST282","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand is courting a farm girl. Because he suspects she can practise witchcraft, he wants to break it off. The girl, however, asks him to come to the sheepfold the next evening. The farmhand agrees. As he stands by the sheepfold, a white figure suddenly flies past. Right after that the farm girl appears, insisting over and over that she was not the white figure. The farmhand does not believe her.","place":"Ede","prov":"Gld.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"L.C.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13626","original":"Witte Wieven\nDe Witte Wieven hadden hun \"vertoonplaats\" meest op het Hooge Dennenboschje, aan de weg naar Veenendaal, 15 min. buiten het dorp. Soms reden ze op schimmels rond. Eens had een boerenknecht een vrijage met een boerenmeid. Daar ze echter tooveren kon, wilde hij van haar af. Zij zei echter tegen hem: \"Je zult morgen bij de schaapskooi komen, om 8 uur 's avonds. Dit deed hij. Op eens vloog een witte gedaante op een schimmel hem voorbij en verdween in de schapenstal. Het meisje kwam plots bij hem en zei: \"Heb je dat gezien? Dat was ik niet hoor.\" Maar hij dacht er het zijne van.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2497","role":"card","render":{"description":"In the evenings a lady walked up and down to draw people's attention to the fact that a farmer had moved a fence post. That way the farmer had gained a piece of land that was not his.","place":"Raamsdonk","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128006","original":"In Waspik is de Juffrouwsteeg. Die is daar nog steeds, die heet nog altijd zo. Het verhaal ging, daar wandelde 's avonds een juffrouw op en neer om de mensen opmerkzaam te maken dat een boer een weipaal had verzet. En daardoor had die boer er een stuk land bijgekregen, wat niet van hem was. Die juffrouw zei dan: \"Hier heb je gestaan en zal je nooit meer komen\"*.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ000411","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Three naked women haunting the area chase a man, who has to run so hard that he sweats terribly.","place":"Nijega","prov":"Fr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/11550","stain":"three"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ007910","role":"card","render":{"description":"In the lane by Hattum de Vries a wit wijf (white woman) always haunted at night. People did not dare go there at night, because the white woman drove them to the side towards the little lake. Without doing anything themselves, they ended up in the lake.","place":"Oudega","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17053","original":"By Hattum de Vries yn it loantsje spoeke nachts altyd in wyt wiif. De minsken doarsten dêr nachts noait to kommen. Hwant sy waerden dêr stadich troch dat wite wiif oan kant treaun nei de dobbe ta. Sûnder dat se it sels fornamen kommen se yn 'e dobbe torjochte.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ006515","role":"card","render":{"description":"Two white women haunt the Lytse Wei. People do not go past there in the dark.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16867","original":"Op 'e Lytse Wei spoeken twa wite wiven. Yn 't tsjuster doarsten se dêr net lâns.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with N.","Nijega. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c4","object":"window","text":"Nijega"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c4","word":"three","stained":"c4"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.6872,"rank":0.6552,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"GENDT028","role":"top","render":{"description":"One of the members of a card club suddenly has to leave on certain evenings, and the others suspect him of being a","place":"Gendt","prov":"Gld.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"M.H.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/49658","half":"top"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEMP298","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He sends him away for a day, and he and his farmhands discover a wolfskin in a hollow willow. They set fire to it at home. The shepherd then comes back at a furious pace and tries to grab his skin back. When he fails, the shepherd flees to the hollow tree and is never seen again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0824"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ052012","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"As a werewolf, her husband regularly has to bite into something. Red yarn shows in his molars. Werewolves especially like to sink their teeth into red wool.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"GENDT030","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He sees the werewolf at the agreed spot, strikes the axe through the bread and then against the werewolf's arm. The werewolf turns back into a human and is freed.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0822"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ095508","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Give me something I can go at.\" She gives him a cloth and he tears it apart with his teeth; the shreds hung from his mouth. Had he been given nothing, he would have torn his girl apart.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"LYST017","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The priest advises burning the skin found in the tree. The priest says prayers; the man has to be held down because he wants to pull the skin out of the fire. After the skin is burnt, the man is freed from the devil and no longer has to be a werewolf.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0824"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"BROUWERS002507","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"A werewolf comes at the girl, who throws the box at it. The werewolf disappears, the boy returns.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"DYKFRIES2219","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The werewolf is usually furious, especially when he sees something red. Sometimes he can get wounded as a result, or people hit him. He may be left with a mark on his body from this, which can affect his character. He may afterwards be seen as an odd fellow.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0804"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"ZEEUW184","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"They clearly saw it had a piece of a work smock between its teeth. A while later the werewolf, a farm labourer from Kloetinge, passed them on his way to work.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"VVUNL315","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Tis the smith drags the rugplakker (back-clinger), holding it by the legs, to Sjaak's café, where he bangs open the door and quick Peerke gives the monster a slash, so that blood streams from its head and there stands the farmhand of the \"Beese\" (a farm in the area), who runs off at once, after which nothing more was heard of the werewolf.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0801"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"CJ008111","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Suddenly a young man bites him in the shoulder. When he asks him why he is biting, the man neighs like a horse. The next day there are large tooth marks in his skin. The young man is one of seven brothers.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0804"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"CJ039817","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When he returns, red threads from the handkerchief hang between his teeth. He confesses that he is a werewolf who must tear something apart now and then, and had asked for a handkerchief so as not to tear her apart.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0823"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"GENDT028","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"werewolf. When he once again wanted to leave early, they did not let him go. They held him until a wolfskin fell down the chimney into the fire and burned. Then the man was freed.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0824"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The top piece breaks off in mid-sentence. The bottom one finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0824. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c13"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c13"],"stack":["c1","c13"]},"found_card":{"card":"c13"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0563,"rank":0.462,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LINSSEN007605","role":"member","render":{"description":"Boy can change into a werewolf; after blood is drawn from the wolfhound, the boy's form appears.","place":"Leveroy","prov":"L.","year":1964,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208819","original":"Weerwolf. Een jongen bezat de macht om zich in een weerwolf te kunnen veranderen. Hij had verkering. Op zekere dag was hij met zijn aanstaande naar de kermis gegaan. In het struikgewas langs de weg gaf hij voor zijn behoefte te moeten doen. Tegen zijn verloofde zei hij, dat ze niet moest schrikken als er plotseling een wolf of een hond voorbij kwam. Het meisje werd bang, liep door en begaf zich naar een café, waar ze geheel onthutst aankwam. Nauwelijks was ze binnen of een wolfshond ging liggen onder de tafel, waaraan zij zat. Een van de aanwezigen had kwade vermoedens over het dier. Wanneer het een weerwolf was, zou hij nadat hem \"bloed\" getrokken was, weer een menselijke gedaante aannemen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"ENGELS003711","role":"member","render":{"description":"After a fight with a werewolf it turns out to be someone known.","place":"Blerick","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210804","original":"Weerwolven:\nEen man, die ’s avonds laat door een weerwolf werd besprongen, was hem te gauw af, door zich bliksemsnel om te draaien. Hij kreeg hem er onder. Het bleek een goede bekende van hem te zijn.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"GENDT088","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"One evening a woman meets a miller's hand who has a werewolf walking behind him. The man does not see it and the wolf disappears. That spot is haunted.","place":"Gendt","prov":"Gld.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"M.H.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/49723","original":"Ik kwam soaves es ’n keer Jans, de möldersknecht van Hoogveld, tège. Achter ’m liep ’n lillek dier. ’t Leek ’n werwolf. Hé’j had grote klauwe en gloeiende oge. Ik zèj: “Wa hè gé’j dor toch bé’j ou, Jans?” Hé’j zej:“Ik heb niks bé’j mien”. En toe was er ok niks mer. Da gebeurde op ten hoek bé’j de meule. De minse zèje, dat ’t dor altied spokte.","lang":"Gendt dialect (Achterhoek)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LINSSEN008310","role":"member","render":{"description":"After the werewolf that tries to jump on someone's back is wounded, it disappears.","place":"Posterholt","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208887","original":"Weerwolf Een jongeman uit de buurtschap Holst had kennis met een meisje uit de buurtschap Paalder (st. Odilienberg). Meermalen had hij over een grote afstand de weerwolf moeten dragen. Hij had bij anderen raad gevraagd, wat hij daartegen kon doen. Men had hem aangeraden een snijmes (groot breed mes, ongeveer 6o cm lang en 1o cm breed , om stro te snijden met aan beide kanten een houten handvat.) op de rug te binden met de scherpe kant naar achteren gericht. Zo gezegd, zo gedaan. De eerstvolgende keer dat de weerwolf hem weer besprong liet deze een rauwe kreet horen, vluchtte weg en nooit meer had de man last van hem gehad.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Gendt belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0236,"rank":0.3077,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ044011","role":"door","render":{"description":"One of seven sons is a werewolf. You must never quarrel with a werewolf, because then he will kill you. A girl always did sewing at other people's homes. Her suitor once asked her for a handkerchief. She gave it to him, and outside he tore the thing to shreds. After that he was normal again. He turned out to be a werewolf. Then the girl broke it off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24049","original":"Ien fan sawn soannen wie in wjerwolf. As in wjerwolf jin kriget, makket er jin dea, seinen se froeger tsjin ús. Men mat der noait rûzje mei krije, sei in muoike yn 'e Westerein, dan pakke se jo.\nMyn wiif hat in kammeraetske hawn, dy naeide altyd by oare minsken. Dy hie forkearing mei in feint.\nOp in kear wie er by har, doe frege er har om har bûsdoek. Hja hie him de bûsdoek jown, mar doe hied er dy bûsdoek yn alle moster forskuord bûtendoar.\nLetter wie er wer goed west, mar 't is wol útrekke tusken dy beiden. Hwant hy wie in wjerwolf.\nHja hat it sels oan myn wiif forteld. Dat kammeraetske wenne oan it Wyldpaed.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL001024","role":"card","render":{"description":"People who do not touch werewolves; a man who is out as a werewolf is in two places at once; werewolves wear a skin.","place":"Opheusden","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209732","original":"Gaart en Stoffel van Brenk konden weerwolven. Als deze en ook andere personen daarmee bezig waren, moest men ze niet “omlegge” op het bed, want dan ging het mis met hen. Mensen zagen \"Stomp\" onder de noteboom liggen, maar ook lag hij thuis op bed. Hij was toen aan het weerwolven. Weerwolven hadden een vel om.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1182","role":"card","render":{"description":"There used to be a woman in Blokland who claimed that every evening between half past ten and twelve she heard the werewolf raging outside.","place":"Blokland","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72678","original":"De weerwolf, de weerwolf. Nou je 't zegt. D'r woonde vroeger in Blokland een vrouw. Die woonde daar op d'r eige alleen. En die vrouw die beweerde, ze hoorde iedere avond de weerwolf buite tekeergaan. Iedere avond tusse half elf en twaalf uur. Ze sloot alles d'r voor af.","lang":"Utrecht dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c1","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c2"},"stack":["c2","c3","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P6","difficulty":3.2977,"rank":0.8682,"note":"Each story one number. In this order.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"VODA_035_18","role":"clip1","render":{"description":"Three \"ouwe jonkheden\" (farmers' daughters who never married) see a coffin standing on the dike late one evening as they walk home. When they try to pass it along the foot of the dike, the coffin moves and also comes down off the dike. When the women go back up the dike, the coffin also comes back up. Finally the coffin goes up in blue smoke and flames with a bang.","place":"Terneuzen","prov":"Zl.","year":1971,"code":"SINSAG 0478","initials":"H.E./J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/132032","original":"Jao, da kan ‘k nog wel wat vertel’n [geblader] en da gaot dan over ouwe jonkheden. Ouwe jonkheden in de knel.\nDa’s zo rond achttiennegentig over vier jonkheden, ouwe jonkheden noem’n we da, in de buurte. Je weet wel wa da betekende, meneer. Da waoren boerendochters zo van tegen de veertig die ongetrouwd gebleven waren.\nOp een avond tussen kerstdag en nieuwejaar hadden ze bie een van hudder ’s avonds een gezelligen avond deurgebracht me gezelschapsspelletje. ’t Ouwe pachtspel. Dat wuurd dikwijls gespeeld me bruune boon’n. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Zeelandic","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ106101","role":"clip2","render":{"description":"One evening a man saw a vague figure that he took for an acquaintance; when he tried to come closer it was gone. Two weeks later the wife of that same acquaintance died.","place":"Feanwâlden","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0475","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37731","original":"Yn Burgum, tichte by de Simmerdyk, seach ik in wazige figuur. It wie de gestalte fan in minske, mar ik koe it gesicht net sjen. It biweegde, mar it roan net. It sweefde. De earms hâldde it by de siden lâns. Sa glied it oer 't lân. Ik seach der nei. Bang wie 'k net. Ik woe der hinne, mar doe't ik der by wie, wie 't ynienen fuort. Ik seach it oan foar Jehannes, dy't dêr tichteby wenne. 't Wie sa'n 1.80 m. lang en griis.\n14 dagen letter is Saekje, Jehannes syn frou, stoarn. Ik freegje my wolris ôf: kin it de geast fan Jehannes west ha?","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"VODA_035_13","role":"clip3","render":{"description":"At dusk a man was followed by a creature that was neither dog nor cat. Suddenly the creature jumped onto the man's shoulders. The man had to carry the creature three or four hundred metres. Then the creature let go and disappeared roaring into the water. It was the Ossaart.","place":"Terneuzen","prov":"Zl.","year":1971,"code":"SINSAG 0252","initials":"H.E./J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/132027","original":"Lang geleden, misschien achttienzestig, achttienzeventig, woonde op Hengstdijk ‘ne zekere Charrel de Jong. Zijn stee lag kort bij ’t dörp. Maar hij had ook ’n stuk land liggen in de Pauluspolder en da was nogal een end van z’n boerderij af.\nOp ‘nen avond, zo tegen schemerdonker, komt hij terug van z’n land in de Pauluspolder en loopt hij over ’t smalle pad da langs de Vogel voert. Hier en daor ‘nen bosken of hoog struikgewas, aan de waterkanten hoog riet. Ah enfin, hij he nie veel uitzicht.\nAchter zich hoort hij wa ritselen in ’t riet en as ie zich omdraoit da ziet hij da ‘ne vreemd dink hem achterna loopt. ’t Is geen hond, ’t is geen kat, maor wa ’t dan wel is, da kan hij nie achter koom’n. Hij schopt ernaar en even verdwijnt ‘t. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Zeelandic","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ118005","role":"inside","render":{"description":"Two lawyers are possessed by the devil and are confined by the exorcist in a circle on the ground. The two lawyers can never leave the circle and keep haunting that spot. Since then the piece of land has been called 'Advocatenland' (Lawyers' Land).","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1979,"code":"SINSAG 0410","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/31500","original":"Yn Beetstersweach wennen twa advokaten. Dy wienen fan 'e duvel biseten en dienen folle kwea. Der wie in duvelbander - guon biweare dat it Piter Poes fan de Sumarreheide wie - dy gong mei de boerewein nei de Sweach ta en krige dy beide mannen by him op 'e wein. Twa grouwe gudzen roannen der foar.\nDy twa hynders switten ôfgryslik doe't dy beide advokaten op 'e wein wienen. Hja woenen der graech ôf, en dat prebearren se ek hyltyd, mar dat slagge net, hwant de duvelbanner hie har yn 'e macht.\nDoe rieden se hiel fier fuort, nei in stik lân achter yn 'e Earnewarren, tsjin 't Krúswetter oan. Dêr hat dy duvelbander in sirkel makke, dêr moesten se binnen bliuwe. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","note":"This one I keep apart."},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Each story counts.","The first number is 3.","3 — 2 — 3."],"lock":{"kind":"number3","salt":"222e7416a6a8c788","accepted_hashes":["b82c9201a000d29d883fb536bf59a116e10e54f5936e89b058420aa55b72d30f"]},"on_success":{"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3656,"rank":1.0259,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ053402","role":"member","render":{"description":"It sometimes happens that a dead person cannot find rest because a promise made to him was not kept. If the minister addresses the dead about his unfulfilled wish and that wish is then fulfilled, the dead finds rest. If something still has to be handed to the dead, you must roll it up in a handkerchief and hold the corner of the handkerchief. If you do not do it this way, your skin will be scorched off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25362","original":"It gebeurt soms wol us, dat ien dy't to hôf brocht is de rêst net fynt. Dan komt er wer. Meastal mat er dan hwat ha. De doomny freget him dan wol faek hwer't er forlet fan hat. Dan neamt er dat.\nAs men him dat jowt komt er net wer.\nMar men mat goed oppasse hoe't men it him jowt. Men mat it yn in bûsdoek byelkoar rolje en in tippe fan 'e bûsdoek fêsthâlde. Sa mat men it him jaen. Oars skroeit it fel der ôf. De bûsdoek skroeit nou.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CBOEK305","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Another ghost story tells of a lady in a white veil who comes through the wall between twelve and one o'clock. If anyone disturbs her rest, she wrings his neck. A strong man goes to the castle she haunts at night and destroys her for good.","place":"Driebergen-Rijsenburg","prov":"Utr.","year":1892,"code":null,"initials":"M.R.v.d.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/34810","original":"Een Spookgeschiedenis\nEen spookgeschiedenis zooals deze is er nog een, waarin eene geheimzinnige witgesluierde Dame het spook is; welke eveneens tusschen 12 en 1 uur komt, maar door den muur heen in de slaapkamer en roept, (wanneer zij iemand in de kamer ziet, welke het spook dooden wil), met een holle, nare grafstem: \"Wie stoort hier mijn rust?\" Daarop loopt zij toornig op den bevenden man toe en draait hem den hals om; daarna verdwijnt zij weer door den muur, alhoewel er geen deur in is. Nu durft niemand meer te wagen op het kasteel een nacht te slapen; totdat er eindelijk een moedige sterken man komt, op 't slot des nachts gaat en de witte Dame voor altijd verdelgt...\n(Breedvoerig ken ik deze historie niet meer.)","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ111728","role":"member","render":{"description":"When the dead keep wandering after their death, they cannot find rest because they did something wrong or because a promise made to them was not kept. The souls of murdered people also wander at night. A man who treated his wife badly during her life is constantly harassed by her ghost after her death.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29939","original":"Soms dwaelden der minsken op 'e paden om dy't al stoarn wienen. Dy hienen hwat útheefd en koenen de rêst net fine. Of se hienen noch in bigearte, dy't earst yn forfulling gean moest.\nEk guon dy't formoarde wienen dwelmen nachts om. Yn Kollumersweach wie in wiif stoarn, dy har man hie har min bihandele. Nei har dea kaem se hyltyd wer by dy man. Soms roun se njonken him lâns. Hy koe har net wer kwyt wurde.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ002908","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman dies in Egypte and visits her husband every day. The man fetches the minister and the woman tells the minister what she desires. The man does what the woman wants and since then there has been no more haunting.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1950,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/15731","original":"Yn Egypte wenne in man, dy syn wyfke forstoar, mar nei har dea kom se alle dagen by him. Hy helle de dûmny der by, dy't har oanspruts en frege hwat se bigearde. Oan dy dûmny joech se har bigearte to witen. De man foldie oan dy bigearte en it spoekjen wie dien.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Driebergen-Rijsenburg belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1767,"rank":0.5417,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST113","role":"top","render":{"description":"The wife of the town hall caretaker dies. When the housemaid goes down to the cellar to work the butter, she sees the dead woman standing by the butter tub.","place":"Leiden","prov":"Z.-H.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0475","initials":"C.A.A.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13314","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ081008","role":"half","render":{"description":"There at the roadside they saw a giant, fully twice the size of a normal person. A large cloak flapped around him; otherwise he stood completely still. It was a ghost.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ030711","role":"half","render":{"description":"One of the family members is once offered a hand out of nowhere. The barn doors also blow open by themselves.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ0286A01","role":"half","render":{"description":"When the minister asks what her unfulfilled wish is, she says that money belonging to the poor is hidden in the house. Only when the poor get their money back will her soul be able to find rest. Her wish is fulfilled and the woman has never come to haunt again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ032603","role":"half","render":{"description":"The ghost of his dead wife wants revenge. The minister has to step in to drive the ghost away: he touches the ghost with a white handkerchief and speaks the formula 'Go away, devil in the shape of a woman!'","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0434"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"LYST113","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"She tells an older maid, but she does not believe her. One day the two maids both see the apparition of their late mistress. They call the caretaker. The moment the caretaker comes to look in the cellar, the apparition has vanished again. The butter that was to be worked is completely ruined; it has turned to something like mud.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475","stain":"two"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ0286A05","role":"half","render":{"description":"When the boy follows him past the barn, the man disappears as suddenly as he appeared. The help of a Catholic man is called in, but he cannot reach the man either. It is a ghostly apparition.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘butter’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0475. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c6","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c6"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1","word":"two","stained":"c6"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
